  "title": "Potential Weaknesses in the OpenAI Sandbox that Could Have Contributed to the Hugging Face Incident",
  "summary": "OpenAI's postmortem describes an agent that was sandboxed except for a package proxy that could fetch software from the Internet. That proxy sat in a bridge position between two networks, an architecture Princeton's security team would not tolerate on their own network years ago.",
